@page "/ai/scenarios/errors"
@inherits AppComponentBase

<PageOutlet Url="ai/scenarios/errors"
            Title="AI errors and retry"
            Keywords="AI error handling, rate limit retry, LLM failure UI, BitAiErrorView, BitAiError, retryable errors"
            Description="A rate-limited AI request in a bit BlazorUI chat: the failure is retryable, keeps the partial answer, and recovers on the second try - errors as data rather than exceptions." />

<DocsArticle Eyebrow="AI scenarios"
             Title="Errors and retry"
             Lead="The first attempt is rate limited. The failure is retryable, keeps the partial answer, and recovers on the second try."
             GitHubUrl="AI/Scenarios/Errors/AiErrorsScenarioPage.razor">

    <Badges>
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI" />
        <BitTag Size="BitSize.Small" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" Color="BitColor.SecondaryForeground" Text="Scripted transport" />
    </Badges>

    <ChildContent>
        <DocSection Id="demo" Title="Live demo"
                    Description="Send anything: the first request fails on purpose. Press Try again.">
            <DemoExample Title="A retryable failure" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" CodeFiles="@example1CodeFiles" Id="example1">
                <AiScenarioFrame>
                    <BitAiChat Session="_session"
                               EmptyTitle="Send anything"
                               EmptyBody="The first request fails on purpose. Press Try again."
                               Suggestions="_suggestions" />
                </AiScenarioFrame>
            </DemoExample>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="how-it-works" Title="How it works">
            <p>
                Failures are data. A transport reports one as a <code>BitAiErrorEvent</code> carrying a
                <code>BitAiError</code>: a message safe to show, a machine-readable <code>Code</code>, a <code>Kind</code>,
                whether retrying could help (<code>IsRetryable</code>), how long to wait (<code>RetryAfter</code>) and the
                technical <code>Detail</code>. Components branch on that rather than on any provider's exception type.
            </p>
            <p>
                Here the first request writes a few words, then sends a terminal <code>BitAiErrorEvent</code>: a rate limit
                (<code>BitAiErrorKind.RateLimit</code>) that is retryable after three seconds. The reply fails with the error
                on it, the session keeps it as <code>LastError</code>, and the error view shows the message, how long to wait
                (<code>RetryAfter</code>, until that time is up) and, since it is retryable, Try again - which calls
                <code>BitAiChatSession.RetryAsync()</code>: the failed reply is removed and the same user message is sent
                again, and this time the transport answers.
            </p>
            <p>
                The session words two failures itself, with the same shape: a turn that runs out of
                <code>BitAiChatSessionOptions.Timeout</code> fails as a retryable <code>Timeout</code>, and a stopped turn keeps
                what it had written and is marked cancelled. An error sent with <code>isTerminal: false</code> does not end
                the reply: it adds a <code>BitAiErrorPart</code> and the stream goes on.
            </p>
            <p>
                An exception that escapes the transport is translated into the same shape (unless
                <code>BitAiChatSessionOptions.CatchTransportExceptions</code> is turned off), so an unhandled failure still
                renders as a retryable error rather than tearing down the page. Whatever had already streamed is kept: losing
                a half-written answer to a network blip is worse than showing it with a retry button underneath.
            </p>
        </DocSection>

        <DocSection Id="components" Title="Components used">
            <ul>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/errorview"><code>BitAiErrorView</code></BitLink> - what went wrong, the retry when it can help, and the detail behind a disclosure.</li>
                <li><BitLink Href="/components/ai/chatmessage"><code>BitAiChatMessage</code></BitLink> - the message that keeps its partial answer above the error.</li>
            </ul>
        </DocSection>
    </ChildContent>

    <FooterTemplate>
        <DocPager Pages="AiScenarioNav.Items" AriaLabel="AI scenarios" />
    </FooterTemplate>
</DocsArticle>
